lisa-design:
- crane tag (go-containerregistry) over oras tag: gooci is built on go-containerregistry, crane reads the same Docker keychain docker/login-action writes, and it installs with `go install` like gooci (no new action, no binary download/checksum step). crane.Tag re-PUTs the raw manifest bytes, so the digest is preserved (proven locally against ggcr's in-memory registry with real gooci v0.0.7 output: two uploads gave two digests, crane tag gave one).
- crane pinned to v0.20.7, not v0.22.1: setup-go exports GOTOOLCHAIN=local, and release-go-plugin.yml uses the caller's go.mod Go version; v0.20.7 is the newest release whose go directive (1.24.0) is no newer than gooci v0.0.7's (1.24), so it cannot break a plugin repo that installs gooci today. v0.21+ need go 1.25.
- Tag from the digest (`crane tag repo@<digest> <tag>`), not from repo:<first tag>, so a concurrent push to the first tag can't redirect the rest; then verify every tag with `crane digest` and fail on any mismatch.
- The first tag from cmd/release is the most specific (vX.Y.Z / main / pr-N); upload goes there only. Single-tag runs (rc, pr-N) still run the verification (no crane tag calls).
- "Tag the rest" is one identical step in all four gooci-upload jobs (preview plugin/policies, release plugin/policies); TestUploadOnceTagTheRest enforces single upload + that step, so a new gooci upload job must adopt it.
- Left alone: plugin-release.yml (legacy, README says unchanged until removed; excluded from these tests like the existing ones), publish-image.yml (one imagetools create with every --tag -> one index already), release-helm.yml (one helm push per release).
